=====================================
SELECTIVE REPEAT ARQ ALGORITHM
=====================================

AIM:
-----
To implement Selective Repeat ARQ
protocol using UDP socket programming in C.

==================================================
SERVER (RECEIVER) ALGORITHM
==================================================

1. Start

2. Declare variables:
   - serverSock
   - frame
   - expected
   - received[]
   - serverAddr
   - clientAddr

3. Create UDP socket.

   serverSock = socket(AF_INET,
                       SOCK_DGRAM,
                       0)

4. Configure server address.

   serverAddr.sin_family = AF_INET
   serverAddr.sin_port = htons(9002)
   serverAddr.sin_addr.s_addr =
            INADDR_ANY

5. Bind socket.

   bind(serverSock,
        (struct sockaddr*)&serverAddr,
        sizeof(serverAddr))

6. Initialize expected frame.

   expected = 0

7. Repeat continuously.

   while(1)

8. Receive frame from sender.

   recvfrom(serverSock,
            &frame,
            sizeof(frame),
            0,
            (struct sockaddr*)&clientAddr,
            &addrSize)

9. Simulate frame loss.

   if(rand() % 10 < 2)

       continue

10. Check whether frame is new.

    if(received[frame] == 0)

11. Mark frame as received.

    received[frame] = 1

12. Else duplicate frame received.

13. Send ACK for received frame.

    sendto(serverSock,
           &frame,
           sizeof(frame),
           0,
           (struct sockaddr*)&clientAddr,
           addrSize)

14. Slide receiver window.

    if(frame == expected)

15. Move expected frame forward.

    while(received[expected] == 1)

         expected++

16. Repeat process.

17. Close socket.

18. Stop

==================================================
CLIENT (SENDER) ALGORITHM
==================================================

1. Start

2. Declare variables:
   - clientSock
   - totalFrames
   - windowSize
   - base
   - next
   - ack
   - ackReceived[]
   - serverAddr

3. Read total number of frames.

   scanf("%d", &totalFrames)

4. Read window size.

   scanf("%d", &windowSize)

5. Create UDP socket.

   clientSock = socket(AF_INET,
                       SOCK_DGRAM,
                       0)

6. Configure server address.

   serverAddr.sin_family = AF_INET
   serverAddr.sin_port = htons(9002)
   serverAddr.sin_addr.s_addr =
            inet_addr("127.0.0.1")

7. Set timeout value.

   tv.tv_sec = 2
   tv.tv_usec = 0

8. Apply timeout to socket.

   setsockopt(clientSock,
              SOL_SOCKET,
              SO_RCVTIMEO,
              &tv,
              sizeof(tv))

9. Initialize sender window.

   base = 0
   next = 0

10. Repeat until all frames are sent.

    while(base < totalFrames)

11. Send frames inside window.

    while(next < base + windowSize
          && next < totalFrames)

12. Send frame to receiver.

    sendto(clientSock,
           &next,
           sizeof(next),
           0,
           (struct sockaddr*)&serverAddr,
           addrSize)

13. Increment next frame number.

    next++

14. Wait for ACK.

    recvfrom(clientSock,
             &ack,
             sizeof(ack),
             0,
             (struct sockaddr*)&serverAddr,
             &addrSize)

15. If ACK received.

    ackReceived[ack] = 1

16. Slide sender window.

    if(ack == base)

17. Move base forward.

    while(ackReceived[base] == 1)

         base++

18. If timeout occurs.

19. Retransmit only lost frames.

    for(i = base; i < next; i++)

       if(ackReceived[i] == 0)

           resend frame i

20. Repeat process.

21. Close socket.

22. Stop

==================================================
PSEUDOCODE
==================================================

SERVER:
--------

Create UDP socket

Bind socket

Repeat forever

    Receive frame

    If frame lost

         Ignore frame

    Else

         Mark frame received

         Send ACK

         Slide receiver window

Close socket


CLIENT:
--------

Read total frames and window size

Create UDP socket

Set timeout

Repeat until all frames sent

    Send frames inside window

    Wait for ACK

    Mark ACK received

    Slide sender window

    If timeout

         Retransmit only lost frames

Close socket

==================================================
KEY RULE
==================================================

If frame N is lost:

Retransmit ONLY frame N

Other correctly received frames
are not retransmitted.

==================================================
ROLES
==================================================

Client  → Sender

Server  → Receiver

